<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug cocoa bean imports down 9.15 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug cocoa bean imports down 9.15 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in August totalled 4,794 tonnes, down by 9.15 percent from 5,277 tonnes a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday. The breakdown is as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Aug 96	     July 96	  Aug 95</p>
<p> Total	   4,794		5,964	    5,277</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana	   3,117		4,725	    4,688</p>
<p> Venezuela	 631		  546		357</p>
<p> Ecuador	   274		  347		 77</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first eight months of calendar 1996 were 37,547 tonnes, against 29,968 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa bean products were as follows (in</p>
<p>tonnes):		Aug 96	 July 96	  Aug 95</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	     167	     193	     192</p>
<p> Defatted paste	   72	     nil	     nil</p>
<p> Cocoa butter	  1,434	   1,356	   1,269</p>
<p> Cocoa powder	    690	     600	     491</p>
<p>Chocolate</p>
<p> confectionery	   909	     920	     970</p>
</text>
